From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Find Buddy's LLVM tools for triton-riscv

The buddy-mlir-llvm RPM installs its LLVM tools (opt, llc, mlir-translate,
clang++) in a private bin directory. Search that directory before PATH so
triton-riscv uses the LLVM toolchain matching buddy-mlir.

The @BUDDY_LLVM_BINDIR@ placeholder is filled in during RPM %prep.

--- a/triton-riscv-9ded1d4c19462dd13a9addef5551a4d09e7e3e97/backend/paths.py
+++ b/triton-riscv-9ded1d4c19462dd13a9addef5551a4d09e7e3e97/backend/paths.py
@@ -61,6 +61,11 @@
     if bundled := _bundled_bin_path(bin_name):
         return bundled

+    # Check the private bin directory supplied by the buddy-mlir-llvm RPM.
+    private_tool = Path("@BUDDY_LLVM_BINDIR@") / bin_name
+    if private_tool.is_file():
+        return str(private_tool)
+
     path_entry = shutil.which(bin_name)
     if path_entry:
         return path_entry
